{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/143754-2-changeling-conditions","id":143754,"title":"2 Changeling Conditions","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-05-20T12:00:57-07:00","id":143754,"title":"2 Changeling Conditions","content":"I decided to convert some old Changeling ideas into Conditions, just to see if I could strike a good balance. Constructive feedback would be appreciated. =)<br /> <br /> <b>Court Enmity</b><br /> <br /> Perhaps you switched Courts, failed to fulfill your Court duties, or abandoned the Court system entirely - or maybe you didn't do anything to deserve censure at all. Whatever the case, you now suffer -2 on any Social rolls with members of a specific Court. If using Social maneuvers against members of your enemy Court, you must open an extra Door. Additionally, you cannot access the social benefits of any Mantle or Court Goodwill rating you may have in that Court until the Condition is resolved. Court Enmity can occur with multiple Courts at once.<br /> <br /> <b>Example Skills</b>: Subterfuge, Socialize<br /> <b>Resolution</b>: The falsehood is openly debunked or your character's name is cleared (often through a challenge such as a major duel, fulfilling a pledgebound quest, or offering an important item).<br /> <b>Beat</b>: n/a<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Forgotten Promise</b><br /> <br /> You have entered into a pledge but do not recall doing so, which leaves you unaware of the parties, restrictions, and boons involved (at least temporarily). The Wyrd will eventually reveal the terms of the deal to you or you can seek them out on your own, but you will have to live up to your end of the bargain or face the consequences. Merits like Common Sense or supernatural powers with similar functions can help you sense when you are about to violate a restriction of a forgotten promise.<br /> <br /> This Condition is usually only available at character creation, though it can stem from a memory-related Condition gained during play, like Amnesia. The player should give input into the pledge's terms, at least about its overall severity and the boon(s) their character was seeking. Storytellers should remain open to amending the terms, should the player have a very negative response.<br /> <br /> <b>Resolution</b>: Your character discovers all of the terms of the pledge.<br /> <b>Beat</b>: A complication arises due to your character's active pursuit of the details of the pledge.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kismet's <a href=\"http://www.wod.kismetrose.com/\" target=\"_blank\">WOD</a> - <a href=\"http://www.dnd.kismetrose.com/\" target=\"_blank\">D&amp;D</a> - <a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/BoundinDreams\" target=\"_blank\">C:tL</a> - <a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/TheNamelessEmpire\" target=\"_blank\">M:tC</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/227-kismetrose","name":"KismetRose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar227_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"110"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-23T17:55:15-07:00","id":147357,"title":"","content":"First, awesome to see someone working on GMC content for Changeling! It's one of my favorite games and I'm happy to see any part of it get a rules update.<br /> <br /> I think Court Enmity could be a Persistent Condition. While Notoriety isn't (which it looks like you modeled this Condition on), I think it'd be neat for players to pick up during character creation. That way, their changelings could have a more significant relationship with Courts they aren't members of/have the Goodwill Merit towards. The Beat could be the usual &quot;whenever it makes you fail a roll.&quot;<br /> <br /> Forgotten Promise is a cool idea. Lots of things Storytellers could potentially do with it, and solving mysteries about their characters is just plain interesting for players. Formatting-wise, it should have (Persistent) after its name, since you're okay with picking it up during characer creation.<br /> <br /> Otherwise, would love to see any further Conditions. Blood and Smoke had a million vampire-related ones, and I'm sure just as many could be done up for changelings.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://blood-and-bourbon.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Blood and Bourbon</a>, my New Orleans-based Vampire chronicle.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3110-false-epiphany","name":"False Epiphany","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3110_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"748"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-23T21:15:18-07:00","id":147537,"title":"","content":"Thank you for the feedback! =)<br /> <br /> I can definitely see making them Persistent conditions (since you could gain Court Enmity as the new guy, even if it's just because you're hanging out with the 'wrong' people in the freehold). I modeled Court Enmity on Notoriety, which seemed like a good fit. It doesn't have an entry for the Beat section, however. Can you tell me why you think Court Enmity should? I'm still trying to learn my way around Conditions and it's a bit more difficult since they're not used in my game yet. Thanks again!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kismet's <a href=\"http://www.wod.kismetrose.com/\" target=\"_blank\">WOD</a> - <a href=\"http://www.dnd.kismetrose.com/\" target=\"_blank\">D&amp;D</a> - <a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/BoundinDreams\" target=\"_blank\">C:tL</a> - <a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/TheNamelessEmpire\" target=\"_blank\">M:tC</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/227-kismetrose","name":"KismetRose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar227_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"110"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-24T19:30:08-07:00","id":148337,"title":"","content":"I hear you on still getting the hang of Conditions. VtM was the only WoD game I was seriously into for a while, and the GMC by comparison has a lot more mechanics to learn your way around. But what's there is pretty awesome! I love how Conditions actively reward players for facing dramatic setbacks.<br /> <br /> On Court Enmity, anyways, the main reason for me is internal consistency; all the other Persistent Conditions grant Beats outside of their resolution, and non-Persistent ones aren't available to players during character creation.<br /> <br /> That also said, it's not like ignoring said rule will cause your game to spontaneously combust (at least, I hope not!), and players would still have incentive to take the Condition since they'll get a Beat upon clearing their changeling's name.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://blood-and-bourbon.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Blood and Bourbon</a>, my New Orleans-based Vampire chronicle.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3110-false-epiphany","name":"False Epiphany","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3110_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"748"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-25T12:20:08-07:00","id":148853,"title":"","content":"Ahhh, I see the rationale now! I'm thinking &quot;Your character backs down from a confrontation or fails a roll due to this Condition&quot; for the beat on Court Enmity, then. Seems to make sense that you might have to take the long way around if you wanted to avoid the social penalty, which would warrant a bit of a reward.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kismet's <a href=\"http://www.wod.kismetrose.com/\" target=\"_blank\">WOD</a> - <a href=\"http://www.dnd.kismetrose.com/\" target=\"_blank\">D&amp;D</a> - <a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/BoundinDreams\" target=\"_blank\">C:tL</a> - <a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/TheNamelessEmpire\" target=\"_blank\">M:tC</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/227-kismetrose","name":"KismetRose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar227_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"110"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-27T09:58:38-07:00","id":150457,"title":"","content":"I don't have all the Condition Cards yet; does anyone know if there's an Insomnia condition written up? Because that seems like something that might affect Changeling games, particularly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kismet's <a href=\"http://www.wod.kismetrose.com/\" target=\"_blank\">WOD</a> - <a href=\"http://www.dnd.kismetrose.com/\" target=\"_blank\">D&amp;D</a> - <a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/BoundinDreams\" target=\"_blank\">C:tL</a> - <a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/TheNamelessEmpire\" target=\"_blank\">M:tC</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/227-kismetrose","name":"KismetRose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar227_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"110"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-27T20:46:01-07:00","id":150990,"title":"","content":"I don't think there's a Condition for insomnia anywhere yet, but Asylum had it as a derangement. Converting it to a GMC game should be pretty easy; heck, you don't need to change any mechanics, just the formatting (since it already explains how to recover).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Insomnia (mild): Your character has trouble getting the required amount of sleep, and not just occasionally. It happens more often than not, and leaves her feeling tired, irritable and unable to concentrate. Any time the character is engaged in a stressful situation (Storyteller discretion), roll Resolve + Composure. Failure means that your character is unable to sleep properly and suffers a \u20132 penalty on all rolls the following day. Each day thereafter is considered \u201cstressful\u201d and requires a similar roll until the character succeeds and gets a full night\u2019s or day\u2019s rest. </div> </div> </div>And totally agreed on insomnia coming up in Changeling games. Getting your dreams meddled with by the fae (in all the many ways they can) can't be good for someone's sleep.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://blood-and-bourbon.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Blood and Bourbon</a>, my New Orleans-based Vampire chronicle.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3110-false-epiphany","name":"False Epiphany","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3110_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"748"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-28T09:03:45-07:00","id":151338,"title":"","content":"So Insomnia practically writes itself. What about a socially-based Condition for being known as an oathbreaker? A Condition for being a Glamour addict? For spending so much time doing dream work that real life starts to feel like a dream? For aging strangely (too fast, too slow), as changelings can do due to Arcadia and Wyrd (at least until they get used to it)? These are just some ideas that sprang to mind.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kismet's <a href=\"http://www.wod.kismetrose.com/\" target=\"_blank\">WOD</a> - <a href=\"http://www.dnd.kismetrose.com/\" target=\"_blank\">D&amp;D</a> - <a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/BoundinDreams\" target=\"_blank\">C:tL</a> - <a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/TheNamelessEmpire\" target=\"_blank\">M:tC</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/227-kismetrose","name":"KismetRose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar227_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"110"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-29T18:14:39-07:00","id":153345,"title":"","content":"Very neat ideas, all! The dreaming Condition in particular seems like it could come up in a lot of games (because really, the dream-shaping aspect of Changeling is just so cool). Here's some stabs at a couple of 'em.<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Oathbreaker (Persistent)</b></span><br /> <br /> Your character made a pledge and broke it. In addition to whatever punishment the oath's sanction carries, your character is shunned by her freehold and suffers a -5 penalty on any Social rolls against changelings who know of her treachery. She will not be granted aid or succor against the True Fae and their servants.<br /> <br /> <b>Resolution</b> The oath's sanction expires, and your character performs a great service to the local freehold that clears her name.<br /> <b>Beat</b> Your character fails a roll because of the Condition, or other changelings refuse to help her when she's threatened by the True Fae.<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><b>Solipsistic (Persistent)</b></span><br /> <br /> Your character believes nothing outside her imagination is real. The world is merely a construct for her amusement. She ignores or reacts bizarrely to situations that don't further her current whims, and suffers a -2 penalty to all Perception, Empathy, and Investigation rolls.<br /> <br /> <b>Resolution</b> Regain a dot of Clarity, lose <i>another</i> dot of Clarity, or achieve an exceptional success on a breaking point.<br /> <b>Beat</b> Your character does something that causes problems for herself (she plucks daisies in the middle of a gunfight, ignores a police officer asking her to pull over, abandons a friend in need, etc.).<br /> <br /> (Somewhat broadened from your original concept of seeing the world as a dream. I can picture it coming up under other circumstances, like prolonged or intimate contact with the True Fae.)<br /> <br /> <br /> Glamour addiction is already nicely modeled by the Addicted and Deprived Conditions. It's handy how broad a lot of them are.<br /> <br /> A few further states of being from the Changeling corebook that seem like potential Conditions me; persistent nightmares, ensorcelled, oathbound, unmasked, the wanderlust and hedge-calling derangements.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://blood-and-bourbon.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Blood and Bourbon</a>, my New Orleans-based Vampire chronicle.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3110-false-epiphany","name":"False Epiphany","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3110_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"748"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-29T20:47:01-07:00","id":153456,"title":"","content":"I like the Solipsistic Condition as it's written! Sounds just nuts enough to be perfect for Changeling. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I would say that most freeholds wouldn't abandon an oathbreaker to the True Fae for breaking minor pledges; if push came to shove, they'd show up, even if they shunned the changeling the rest of the time. I'd keep that last option for those who break the freehold pledge and/or a major pledge (with high values and grave tasks/boons).<br /> <br /> I'll have to take another look at those states from the core book. It's been a while since I've read them, but they might already be in good enough shape for easy conversion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kismet's <a href=\"http://www.wod.kismetrose.com/\" target=\"_blank\">WOD</a> - <a href=\"http://www.dnd.kismetrose.com/\" target=\"_blank\">D&amp;D</a> - <a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/BoundinDreams\" target=\"_blank\">C:tL</a> - <a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/TheNamelessEmpire\" target=\"_blank\">M:tC</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/227-kismetrose","name":"KismetRose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar227_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"110"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-29T21:16:33-07:00","id":153467,"title":"","content":"Thanks! I love how self-balanced the Condition rules let it turn out. Rather than finagle a system for when a changeling should act nuts, her player just gets a reward whenever she chooses to.<br /> <br /> That's a good point on abandoning a changeling over minor broken pledges. I was going by what the core book about oath-breaking, but upon considering, would that really apply to <i>every</i> broken promise? Better to leave it to individual situations/Storyteller judgment than a catch-all Condition, and if you're asking your freehold-mates for help there'll probably be a Social roll anyway (so being an oathbreaker still bites you in the butt).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://blood-and-bourbon.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Blood and Bourbon</a>, my New Orleans-based Vampire chronicle.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3110-false-epiphany","name":"False Epiphany","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3110_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"748"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-30T14:51:38-07:00","id":154193,"title":"","content":"When I get done with the last bit of work I'm doing on the dreaming rules and with prepping for our next session, I'll probably come back to this to see about other Conditions. They're fun. =)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kismet's <a href=\"http://www.wod.kismetrose.com/\" target=\"_blank\">WOD</a> - <a href=\"http://www.dnd.kismetrose.com/\" target=\"_blank\">D&amp;D</a> - <a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/BoundinDreams\" target=\"_blank\">C:tL</a> - <a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/TheNamelessEmpire\" target=\"_blank\">M:tC</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/227-kismetrose","name":"KismetRose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar227_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"110"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-31T21:59:25-07:00","id":155441,"title":"","content":"Some good stuff, here!<br /> <br /> I don't know that I agree with the &quot;nobody will help you against the True Fae&quot; part of Oathbreaker. I mean, yeah, people will definitely shun you if you're a known oathbreaker, but standing by and consigning someone to Arcadia again? That's a hard sell for me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1168-hobbitguy1420","name":"HobbitGuy1420","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"332"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}